      "excerpt": "All Blacks beat Bulls 50-19 \u2013 see how African bookmakers price the match and what it means for your betting strategy.",
      "body": "**All Blacks storm past Bulls 50\u201119 \u2013 a betting playbook for Africa**\n\nThe latest headline that\u2019s been buzzing across the continent is the All Blacks\u2019 50\u2011point demolition of the Bulls in their final tune\u2011up before the South Africa tests. As *Yahoo Sports* reports, New\u202fZealand ran the ball and ran the numbers, leaving Pretoria\u2019s defence flat\u2011footed. For African bettors, this match is more than a historic win \u2013 it\u2019s a goldmine of betting opportunities.\n\n### Why the All Blacks win matters\n\nThe All Blacks have long been a benchmark for New\u202fZealand rugby, but the sheer margin of victory shows they are in top form. For South Africa fans, the loss is a wake\u2011up call ahead of the upcoming test series, and for global punters, the result gives the bookmakers a clear picture of where the action should be. Betting markets for international rugby are now tightening, and the odds are trading around 1.55 for a Black\u2011bush win, 2.70 for a Bulls win, and 1.85 for the over 40.5 points market. These figures are illustrative of what you\u2019ll find on the leading African platforms.\n\n### Odds comparison \u2013 what the bookmakers are saying\n\n| Market | Bet9ja | Sportybet | 1xBet |\n|--------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| All Blacks win | 1.55 | 1.60 | 1.58 |\n| Bulls win | 2.70 | 2.80 | 2.75 |\n| Over 40.5 points | 1.85 | 1.90 | 1.88 |\n| Under 40.5 points | 1.95 | 1.90 | 1.92 |\n\nThe spread is tight, but the slight edge on Bet9ja for the All Blacks win makes it a tempting market for those who trust the home\u2011ground advantage and the team\u2019s recent form. Sportybet offers a slightly higher price for the Bulls win, which could appeal to value\u2011hunters looking for a safer bet on the underdog.\n\n### Betting angles for African punters\n\n1. **Pick the winner** \u2013 With the All Blacks\u2019 dominant performance, the 1.55 odds on Bet9ja give a decent return for a straight win bet. The margin is slim, but the confidence in the team\u2019s form is high.\n\n2. **Over/Under points** \u2013 The 50\u2011point scoreline confirms that the match will likely stay above the 40.5\u2011point line. Bet9ja\u2019s 1.85 odds for the over offer a solid risk\u2011reward balance.\n\n3. **Half\u2011time/Full\u2011time** \u2013 The All Blacks were in front at every half\u2011time check, making a full\u2011time win a safe choice. If you\u2019re looking for a higher payout, consider a double\u2011chance market that covers the All Blacks win or a draw.\n\n4. **Prop bets** \u2013 Look for markets on individual player milestones such as \u201cmost points scored\u201d or \u201cmost tries.\u201d The All Blacks\u2019 forwards, especially the flankers, are likely to cross the 50\u2011point threshold.\n\n### How this fits into the bigger betting landscape\n\nWhile the All Blacks\u2013Bulls game is a marquee event, other stories are also shaping betting trends across Africa:\n\n* **Jaylen Brown\u2019s trade to the 76ers** \u2013 *Sporting News* highlights the pressure Brown faces in Philadelphia. NBA markets are heating up for the 2026\u201127 season, with the 76ers\u2019 odds moving around 1.70 for a win in the opening game.\n\n* **Shedeur Sanders\u2019 first preseason start** \u2013 *Yahoo Sports* tracks his performance against the Bears. College football markets are getting active, and the first\u2011quarter play\u2011calling can drive the over/under on early games.\n\n* **Espanyol\u2019s Monchi on the Championship** \u2013 *BBC Sport* praises the English league as a talent hub. European markets are adjusting to new transfer windows, with odds for teams like Espanyol rising as potential signings emerge.\n\n* **Jo\u00e3o Cancelo\u2019s Barcelona hints** \u2013 *Yahoo Sports* reports on the Portuguese star\u2019s speculations. Transfer markets in Europe are volatile, and betting on future moves can offer long\u2011term value.\n\n### African bookmaker comparison\n\nBeyond Bet9ja, Sportybet, and 1xBet, other African platforms such as Betway, Hollywoodbets, and Melbet are also offering competitive odds on international rugby. For example, Betway\u2019s All Blacks win odds hover around 1.56, while Hollywoodbets offers 1.57. The differences may seem small, but over large volumes they add up.\n\nWhen placing bets, consider the payment method that best fits your region\u2014M\u2011Pesa and MTN MoMo are popular in Kenya, while MTN MoMo and OPay dominate Nigeria. For South Africa, PayPal and instant deposits via credit card are common, and in Ghana, PalmPay and MTN MoMo are the go\u2011to options.\n\n### Responsible gambling\n\nBetting should be fun, not a problem. Set a budget before you start and stick to it. If you\u2019re spending more than you can afford to lose, take a break or seek help. African regulators are tightening the rules on responsible gambling, and many bookmakers now offer tools such as deposit limits, time\u2011out options, and self\u2011exclusion. If you feel you\u2019re out of control, reach out to a local support group or a helpline.\n\n### FAQ\n\n**Q: What is the best market to bet on for the All Blacks vs Bulls?**  \nA: The All Blacks win or the over 40.5 points markets offer the most value, given the team\u2019s recent form and the scoreline.\n\n**Q: Can I use M\u2011Pesa to bet on international rugby?**  \nA: Yes. Most African bookmakers, including Bet9ja and Sportybet, accept M\u2011Pesa deposits in Kenya and Nigeria.\n\n**Q: Are there any special promotions for this match?**  \nA: Many bookmakers run \u201cbet\u2011and\u2011win\u201d offers or free\u2011bet promotions around international fixtures. Check the promotions page on your chosen bookmaker.\n\n**Q: How does the All Blacks\u2019 win affect future test series odds?**  \nA: The result will likely lower the odds for South Africa in the upcoming test series, as bookmakers adjust for the perceived shift in team strength.\n\n### Take the next step\n\nWith the All Blacks\u2019 50\u2011point triumph and the odds now set, there\u2019s never been a better time for African punters to place a stake. Compare the markets, read the odds, and choose the platform that offers the best value and payment convenience.\n\nHead over to sifufinds.com to compare odds, find the best promotions, and start betting responsibly today.\n\n*18+ | Bet Responsibly | T&Cs Apply*",
